{{define "content" -}}
<div class="page-head">
  <h1 id="login-title">Sign in</h1>
  <p>You need an account to claim a handle and download a credential. Signing in is also the only thing catlog ever asks an identity provider for.</p>
</div>

<div id="login-choices">
  {{- range .Data.IdPs}}
  <article class="login-choice panel">
    <a id="login-{{.Key}}" href="{{.Start}}" class="button">Continue with {{.Name}}</a>
    <p>{{.Note}}</p>
  </article>
  {{- end}}
</div>

<article id="login-privacy" class="panel prose" style="margin-top: 1.5rem">
  <header><strong>What catlog learns about you</strong></header>
  <p>
    A single opaque identifier, hashed before it is stored. <strong>catlog never asks for your email address</strong>
    and never receives one — not from Discord, not from Google, not from GitHub.
    <a href="/docs/privacy">The privacy page</a> explains exactly how.
  </p>
</article>
{{- end}}
